  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   - **Central Idea**: Combine multi-resolution optimization with Fourier basis projection to enforce periodicity constraints. Unlike previous strategies, we focus on structural properties (periodicity) that are inherent in optimal solutions.\n   - **Key Rationale**: The Erd\u0151s problem's optimum likely has periodic structure. Fourier projection enables dimensionality reduction and gradient-based optimization while maintaining structural integrity. Cross-validation between coarse/fine resolutions helps escape local optima.\n   - **Bottleneck Addressed**: Current method's slow convergence due to non-periodic constraint enforcement and $\\ell_2$-based projection. Our approach provides $O(1)$ dimensionality reduction via Fourier projection.\n   - **Limitations**: Assumes periodicity, which may not be optimal; requires careful hyperparameter tuning and has spectral convergence issues (\\cite{borovykh2014periodic}).\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   - **Representation**: $h(x) = \\sum_{k=0}^{K} a_k \\cos(2\\pi k x / P) + b_k \\sin(2\\pi k x / P)$\n   - **Variables**: Fourier coefficients $(a_k, b_k)$ for $k=0,\\ldots,K$, amplitude scaling factor $c \\in [0, C_{max}]$\n   - **Objective**: $\\min \\max_{k} \\iint h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\\,dx$\n     - Smoothed version: $C_{smooth} = \\exp(-\\alpha \\max_k \\text{overlap}_k) + \\beta \\|\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}\\|_1$\n   - **Constraints**:\n     - Integral: $\\sum_{i=1}^{n} h_i \\cdot dx = 0.5$\n     - Bounds: $0 \\leq \\operatorname{Re}(h) \\leq 1, 0 \\leq \\operatorname{Im}(h) \\leq 1$\n   - **Formulation**:\n     - Projection: $h_{\\text{proj}} = \\mathcal{F}^{-1}( \\mathcal{F}(h_0) \\odot \\mathcal{W}(\\omega) )$\n     - Optimization: Gradient descent on $(a_k, b_k)$ minimizing sparse correlation matrix $\\mathbf{L}$\n     - $\\mathbf{L} = \\text{Toeplitz}(L_{0}, \\ldots, L_{2K}$)\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   - **Phase 1: Initialization** (20% budget)\n     - Validate initial_h_values against constraints.\n     - Compute Fourier transform: Spectrum_425 = \\text{np.fft.fft}(initial_h_values * dx^{-1})$\n     - Set initial peaks from sorted spectrum: Top 10 components\n     - Define base period candidates: $P \\in \\{0.4, 0.5, 2/3, 0.6\\}$\n   - **Phase 2: Fourier Projection** (30% budget)\n     - Choose active modes $K$ from importance vector.\n     - Projection: $\\mathbf{v}_k = \\{ \\cos(2\\pi k x / P), \\sin(2\\pi k x / P)\\}$\n     - Initialize coefficients $\\mathbf{a}, \\mathbf{b}$ randomly.\n     - Project initial_h_values onto $K$-dimensional space.\n     - Orthogonal projection matrix: $\\mathbf{M} = \\mathbf{v} \\mathbf{v}^T$\n     - Sparse coding: $h = \\mathbf{M} \\mathbf{c}$\n   - **Phase 3: Multi-Resolution** (40% budget)\n     - Coarse-to-fine sweep with $n \\rightarrow 2n$: Scale all periods $\\times \\sqrt{2}$\n     - Gram matrix construction: $\\mathbf{G} = \\mathbf{v}' \\mathbf{v}'^T$\n     - ADMM optimization with dual variables $\\boldsymbol{\\lambda}$:\n       $\\min_{\\mathbf{c}}, \\boldsymbol{\\lambda} \\| \\mathbf{G} \\mathbf{c} - d \\|_2 + 0.5 \\|\\boldsymbol{\\lambda}\\|_2 + c\\|\\mathbf{c}\\|_1$\n     - Check feasibility via projected gradients\n   - **Phase 4: Local Refinement** (10% budget)\n     - Newton-CG on projected correlation matrix:\n       $\\nabla_c \\mathbf{\\ell} = \\text{diag}(\\lambda) (\\mathbf{G}^T \\max_{i} \\partial L_i$\n     - Clip solutions to $[0,1]^n$ using element-wise projection\n     - Final evaluation via direct correlation check\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n   - **Period Selection**: Biased toward periods that minimize autocorrelation in initial solution\n   - **Regularization**: $\\beta \\in \\{0.05, 0.1, 0.2\\}$ scheduled by decreasing $\\alpha$\n   - **Adaptive Modes**: K_recurse from base $K=50$ to $K=500$ in doubling steps\n   - **Random Resampling**: Layered stochastic Gram matrix $\\Omega$ construction\n   - **Geometry Adapation**: Rotation matrix $R_k = \\mathbf{I} + \\text{skew}(\\theta_k)$ for cross-terms\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n   - $t_i$: Time per execution\n   - $T_{total} = 0.3 \\sum_{i} t_i$: Coarse-to-fine weighted sum\n   - Memory: $\\mathcal{O}(n K^2)$ with active caching of $(P_k, K_k)$ pairs\n   - Convergence checks: Jacobian verification every 100 steps\n   - Fallback: Return median of last 5 per-period solutions\n   - Stability: Clip gradients $\\|\\nabla c\\| \\leq 1e3$ and adjust integration step\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n   - **Feasibility Checks**:\n     - Integral: $\\| \\sum h_i \\cdot dx - 0.5 \\| < \\epsilon_1 = 1e-4$\n     - Bounds: $h_i \\in [0,1] \\forall i$, $\\epsilon_2=1e-6$\n   - **Objective Consistency**: Smooth $\\ll$ True max by $<1e-3$\n   - **Validation Checks**:\n     - Four sampled shifts by MPSolver\n     - $\\partial C / \\partial k = \\max_k |\\operatorname{overlap}_k| < 1e-2$\n     - Fourier density: $90\\%$ energy in $\\lfloor K \\rfloor$ modes\n   - **Output Format**: (h_array, c5_score, n) where\n     - h_array: $\\in [0,1]^{n}$ with sum(dx)=0.5\n     - c5_score: $\\max_k \\text{overlap}_k \\cdot dx$\n   - **Sanity Checks**:\n     - Initial score $>0.38$\n     - Monotonic improvement $(\\Delta \\geq -1e-4)$ \n     - No degenerate solutions ($K \\geq 1$)",
